      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "## Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor: Comprehensive Deployment Guide\n\n**I. Introduction and Component Identification**\n*   **Product Designation:** Nexus-7 Proximity Sensor.\n*   **Core Functionality:** Provides precise proximity detection capabilities.\n*   **Electrical Specifications:** Requires a stable 5V DC power supply for optimal performance.\n\n**II. Physical Mounting Protocol**\n*   **Mounting Hardware:** The sensor unit is designed for secure integration using M3 screws.\n*   **Mounting Locations:** Utilize the pre-drilled M3 screw holes situated at the four corners of the sensor housing.\n*   **Installation Best Practices:** Ensure the sensor is firmly seated to maintain signal integrity during operation.\n\n**III. Detailed Wiring and Pinout Schema**\n*   **Pin Assignment Matrix:** A clear mapping of the four available pins is provided below.\n    *   Pin 1: VCC (Voltage Common Collector) – Connect to +5V.\n    *   Pin 2: GND (Ground Reference) – Connect to system ground.\n    *   Pin 3: Signal Output – Connect to the receiving microcontroller input.\n    *   Pin 4: Shield (EMI Protection) –",
      "source": "target",
